{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>ויתמרמר</b> — from the stem of שימי לך תמרורים (Jeremiah 6:17, \"set up warning-signs\")." "<b>ונלחם עמו</b> — meaning that \"him\" is the king of the north, as in: ותראהו את הילד (Exodus 2:6, \"she saw him, the child\"), and: והוא צוה לי אחי (1 Samuel 20:29, \"he commanded me, my brother\")." "<b>והעמיד</b> — the king of the south [stood up] a great multitude." "<b>ונתן</b> — the multitude of the king of the north into his hand." "<b>ונשא</b> — the multitude of the one who is weakened." "<b>והפיל רבואות</b> — from the multitude of the king of the south." "<b>ולא יעוז</b> — the king of the south."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:21:03.574317505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}